# SAVO code ownership
#
# Every file in this repository is owned by the maintainer. Read together with
# the `Protect SAVO code` ruleset (see docs/repository-protection.md), this is
# what makes "nobody changes code without the owner" true rather than a promise:
#
#   * `CODEOWNERS` decides *who* must review a pull request that touches a path.
#   * The ruleset decides that a pull request is the only way onto `main`.
#
# Neither is a courtesy. A review request that nobody can satisfy blocks the
# merge, so keep this list to people who actually maintain the project.
#
# Syntax: <pattern> <owner>...   (later, more specific lines win)

# Everything, by default.
*                       @zyven202-source

# The rules that protect the code are themselves code. Changing them changes the
# guarantee, so they are called out separately to make such a pull request
# obvious in review.
/.github/               @zyven202-source
/scripts/protect-repo.mjs @zyven202-source
/docs/repository-protection.md @zyven202-source

# Anything that can reach data or secrets deserves a slower read.
/supabase/              @zyven202-source
/src/services/          @zyven202-source
/src/integrations/      @zyven202-source
